<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <title>Connect your Spotify account</title>
    <style>
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        background: #0b0f16;
        color: #f4f7fa;
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      }
      .card {
        max-width: 440px;
        margin: 24px;
        padding: 28px;
        border: 1px solid #1c2634;
        border-radius: 16px;
        background: #111823;
      }
      h1 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 20px; }
      p { color: #93a7bb; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; }
      .warning {
        margin: 20px 0;
        padding: 14px 16px;
        border: 1px solid rgba(242, 11, 24, 0.35);
        border-radius: 10px;
        background: rgba(242, 11, 24, 0.1);
        color: #f4f7fa;
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      .warning strong { color: #ff1723; }
      .btn {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 4px;
        padding: 12px 20px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: #ff1723;
        color: #fff;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
      }
      .btn:hover { background: #f20b18; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="card">
      <h1>Connect your Spotify account</h1>
      <p>
        This invite is for Spotify account
        <strong><%= @invite.spotify_user_id %></strong>. It links that
        account so its recently played tracks show up on the feed — nothing
        else (not playlists, not the library).
      </p>

      <p class="warning">
        <strong>Make sure this browser is signed in to Spotify as that account</strong>.
        Spotify's next screen reuses whatever Spotify account is already
        logged in here — it will not ask you to pick one. Signing in as
        anyone else will fail: the callback checks the account against this
        invite. On a shared or borrowed device, sign out of Spotify first or
        open this link in a private/incognito window.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "Continue to Spotify", spotify_join_path(token: params[:token], confirmed: true), class: "btn" %>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
